Package: ssh3-rust-server
Version: @VERSION@-1
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: nagual2 <912140+nagual2@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: systemd, libcrypt1
Homepage: https://github.com/nagual2/ssh3-rust
Description: SSH3 server (Rust implementation) - SSH over QUIC/HTTP-3
 The Rust implementation of the SSH3 server: the SSH3 protocol carried over
 HTTP/3 (QUIC) with the RFC 9220 extended CONNECT. Public keys authenticate
 out of the box; password login is off by default and can be turned on with
 --enable-password-login (or with SSH3_ENABLE_PASSWORD_LOGIN=1 in
 /etc/ssh3/ssh3-rust-server.env). The root account never authenticates by
 password.
 .
 The daemon starts as root and drops to the uid/gid of the authenticated
 user for every session. The systemd unit is installed as
 /usr/lib/systemd/system/ssh3-rust-server.service and the instance
 configuration as /etc/ssh3/ssh3-rust-server.env; both are shipped by this
 package.
 .
 This package is the second implementation of SSH3: the shipped product is
 the Go implementation of nagual2/ssh3-go, this Rust line is the independent
 reference implementation of the protocol.
